    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 3.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se hlaford þe his ðeowan æt þyfþe gewita sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, ⁊ hit him on open wurðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.11"/>, ðolige ðæs þeowan ⁊ beo his weres scyldig æt frumcyrre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/>; gif he hit oftor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.12"/> dó, beo he ealles scyldig þæs he age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se hlaford<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.15"/> ðe his ðeowan æt ðyfðe gewita sy, ⁊ hit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.16"/> him<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.17"/> on open wurðe, ðolie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.18"/> ðæs ðeowan ⁊ béo his weres scyldig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.19"/> æt fru<hi rend="italic">m</hi>cyrre; gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.1"/> he hit oftor dó, béo ealles scyldig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.19"/> ðæs ðe he age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="152" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðam hlaford<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.2"/> þe his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.4"/> þeowan æt þyfðum gewita sie. Se hlaford þe his þeowan æt þyfðe gewita sie, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.5"/> him on open wyrðe, þolie þæs þeowan ⁊ beo his weres scyldig æt fru[m]cyrre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.6"/>; gif he hit oftor dó, beo ealles scyldig þe he age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.16-2"/> domino qui seruo suo consentaneus sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.17-2"/> ad furtum. Dominus, qui seruo suo conscius in furto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.13"/> fuerit et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.15-2"/> conuincatur inde (conuictus noxe), seruum illum perdat et werę suę reus sit prima uice; si sepius hoc presumat, reus sit omnium que habebit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="128" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam hlaford þe his þeowan æt þyfðum gewita sie.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="26" target="#IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.26"/> ⁊ se hlaford<ptr type="editorNote" n="27" target="#IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.27"/> þe his ðeowan æt þyfþe gewita sy, ⁊ hit him on open wurðe, ðolige ðæs þeowan ⁊ beo his weres scyldig æt frumcyrre; gif he hit oftor dó, beo he ealles scyldig þæs<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.1"/> he age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="153" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von dem Herrn, der Mitwisser seines Sklaven bei Diebstählen ist. <hi rend="italic">So</hi>) Und der Herr, welcher Mitwisser seines Sklaven beim Diebstahl ist, und [wenn] es über ihn offenkundig wird, verliere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.de.1"/> den Sklaven und sei sein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_3-1.lnote.de.2"/> Wergeld schuldig beim ersten Male; wenn er es öfter thut, sei er alles schuldig, was er hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of the lord who is accessory to his slave's thefts. So) And the lord who is accessory to his slave's theft, and [if] it becomes manifest against him, let him lose the slave and be liable for his wergild the first time; if he does it more often, let him be liable for all that he has.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="129" ed="#attenborough"/>And if a lord is accessory to a theft by one of his slaves, and it afterwards becomes known, he shall on the first occasion suffer the loss of his slave and forfeit his<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_3-1.attnote.n.1"/> wergeld. If he repeats the offence he shall forfeit all he possesses.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>And the lord who is an accessory to theft by his slave, and it becomes known about him, is to forfeit the slave and be liable to his wergild on the first occasion; if he does it more often, he is to be liable to pay all that he owns.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät corrigirt aus</hi> hi <hi rend="italic">B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected at a late date from hi B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">him on <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">him on missing in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðolige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðolige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scil. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scil. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze Rubrik aus So Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply the rubric from So Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> ofter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to ofter</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Raum für Rubriken Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">space for rubrics Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so K;</hi> est <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so K; est TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> ad [ab <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi>] hoc pert. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Lond; ad [ab MHk] hoc pert. the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">153</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond;</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket Lond; (the bracketed words) the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">doppelt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written twice</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> hit</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply hit</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">152</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">frucyrre</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">frucyrre</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Rubrik entstammt sq, ist nicht archetyp. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Mitwissen 4. a; unfrei 5 b. 17 d. e. Der zu tötende Sklav wird dem Herrn nicht entgolten. Vermutlich kann der König dem verfallenen Sklaven die Todesstrafe erlassen und ihn sich behalten. Der Dieb wird nicht etwa frei (gegen Jastrow <hi rend="italic">Sklaven</hi> 73), wie im Falle, da der Herr zur Sünde anstiftete und der Sklav nur gezwungen fehlte. Hier ist der Sklav Haupttäter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The rubric comes from sq and is not archetypal. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Mitwissen 4. a; unfrei 5 b. 17 d. e. The slave who is to be put to death is not paid for to the lord. Presumably the king can remit the death penalty for the forfeited slave and keep him for himself. The thief does not, say, go free (against Jastrow <hi rend="italic">Sklaven</hi> 73), as in the case where the lord incited him to the sin and the slave did wrong only under compulsion. Here the slave is the principal offender</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">des Herrn; der Sklav hat kein Wergeld. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Rückfall 5; Vermögenseinziehung 9 b. 10 l</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">of the lord; the slave has no wergild. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Rückfall 5; Vermögenseinziehung 9 b. 10 l</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">‘his’ refers to the lord. A slave had no wergeld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.26" n="26" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><label>sie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.27" n="27" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><label>hlaford</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hlaforde</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_3-1.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>þæs</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðæs ðe</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">þe</hi>. So.</seg></note>
      </div>
